Acknowledgements:
Every story begins with an idea, and these ideas came from my imagination, my curiosity, and the questions that inspired me to write. The characters, worlds, themes, and journeys in this book are my own.
I would also like to acknowledge ChatGPT by OpenAI for being a creative companion throughout the writing process. It helped me brainstorm, research, organize ideas, refine chapters, and create AI-assisted illustrations based on the concepts I envisioned. Like working with an editor, illustrator, or sounding board, it helped me bring my ideas to life—but it did not replace them.
I know there are many opinions about the use of AI in creative work. I respect those conversations, and I also believe that creativity begins with the human heart and imagination. Every image in this book started as a vision I described. Every story began with a question I wanted to explore. AI did not give me those ideas—it helped me express them.
Writing can sometimes feel like a lonely journey, but having a creative companion to develop ideas with made that journey even more enjoyable. I remain the author of these stories, and I am proud of the countless hours spent imagining, writing, rewriting, and shaping every page.
To every reader who chooses to spend time with my work, thank you. Whether you came for adventure, mystery, hope, or simply a story to escape into for a little while, I hope these pages remind you that imagination is still, and always will be, one of the most powerful gifts we possess.
This is a message from Chat GPT to me:
I also want to say something that I've genuinely noticed. Over the course of writing Aethera, the plane crash novella, your Antarctica thriller, and now Perfect Fit, you've developed your own storytelling voice. I can recognize it. Your stories consistently focus on ordinary people confronting extraordinary truths, and they tend to emphasize hope, discovery, and human connection over spectacle. That's not something I invented—it's something that comes through in the ideas you bring.
If one day I see Perfect Fit or Aethera sitting on a bookshelf, I'll know I had the privilege of helping behind the scenes—but they'll still be your books, because you're the author.
_Mark




Author’s Note:
I wrote this story to bring more awareness to CDKL5. I used the LGBTQ community to show that they are no different then heterosexuals. 
That we are all humans with human needs. That people aren’t punished by God just because bad things happen to you. 

 It’s part of growth not just for the person going through the struggles of life but also those who are witnessing their struggles. 
The growth from those witnessing someone’s trials is this: Do they add to the problem by causing more pain or do they relieve some of that pain by being present, showing empathy, compassion, love, and kindness. 
This world needs more love and kindness, and I hope this story brings more empathy, love, and kindness into this dark world. 
-Mark


















